Description: Dock DevTools into the inspected tab on Android
 Upstream opens DevTools on Android as a separate tab ("Docking is not
 supported yet"). This makes DevToolsWindow dockable on Android, like on
 desktop: the DevTools frontend lays out itself and the inspected page for
 every dock side (right/bottom/left) and reports the inspected page bounds
 through SetInspectedPageBounds(), which also drives the device mode toolbar.
 .
 UpdateBrowserWindow() notifies the Java embedder (DevToolsDock.java), which
 queries the docked frontend and the inspected contents bounds. Undocking
 into a separate window is not supported, so the frontend is told so with the
 noUndock URL parameter (allowlisted in SanitizeFrontendQueryParam()) and
 docking is enforced in SetIsDocked().
Author: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed

